WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.600
And don't rush into downloading any editing software.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.700
All I'm going to use is Higgsfield Katana inside Claude.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.220
Start by opening Claude and selecting Opus 5.5.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.540
Then connect Higgsfield Katana through MCP

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:13.100
and add our clipping skill.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.460
I'll leave the setup links in the description.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.240
Now Higgsfield Katana guides the editing workflow

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:19.880
so you can just describe what you want

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:21.720
without explaining every cut and transition.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.680
Once you're connected, you can give Claude your footage

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:25.880
or just a link to your video,

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.440
maybe a reference and the music you want to use.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:30.680
But a bad reference can mean a bad result,

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.940
so pick one that fits the style you want.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.460
Check the views, likes, and shares too.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.080
And read the comments to see what people are reacting to.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.240
So in your prompt, tell Claude how long the edit should be

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:42.800
and ask for a vertical video.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:44.700
Then ask for a strong opening,

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:46.400
pacing that matches the reference

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.380
and cuts synced to your music.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.260
I'm also asking for a quick report after each stage

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:54.060
so I can check the direction and make changes as I go.
